                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d4deddd-038a-31f7-acfa-7064214d9098",
                                        "entry_id": "ffad2724-1057-3fa6-8358-6b499be892dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A citizen of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b28e134-90af-4238-b342-22d45a12d5f0",
                                                "sense_id": "4d4deddd-038a-31f7-acfa-7064214d9098",
                                                "text": "The major obstacle to a border settlement is the status of Heixiazi, a 330-square kilometer island at the confluence of the Amur and Ussuri rivers. The island is claimed by the Chinese but controlled by the USSR. Because Heixiazi overlooks Khabarovsk as well as the point where the Trans-Siberian Railway crosses the Amur River, the Soviets are reluctant to give it up."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f75ab063-bffc-39d1-b7af-b1863a00ddad",
                                        "entry_id": "ffad2724-1057-3fa6-8358-6b499be892dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of soviet (“workers' council”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d74dd1f7-3534-455d-ba0e-ac58e85c5877",
                                                "sense_id": "f75ab063-bffc-39d1-b7af-b1863a00ddad",
                                                "text": "Толчками и скачками дело все же идет к тому, что давно провозглашенный нашей партией переход власти к Советам будет осуществлен."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Soviet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9d92ffe-ecde-375d-8dc3-cee2e3219181",
                                        "entry_id": "bae478e3-cc06-30b1-803e-874d679236d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to the Soviet Union or its constituent republics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60b0634e-2a37-45d3-9919-05f75407c990",
                                                "sense_id": "f9d92ffe-ecde-375d-8dc3-cee2e3219181",
                                                "text": "Later, in the 1980s, western scholars found that, notwithstanding the substantial Soviet military buildup near the Chinese borders in the late 1960s, it was Beijing that initiated the clash on Zhenbao (Damanski) Island."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3b64327-346f-4f18-81de-fd779a00c593",
                                                "sense_id": "f9d92ffe-ecde-375d-8dc3-cee2e3219181",
                                                "text": "A monument to Soviet dictator Josef Stalin erected in Moscow's metro is stirring debate, with some Russians welcoming it as a historical tribute, but others saying it's a mistake to commemorate someone who presided over so much suffering."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d670df6c-a18c-3ace-95c3-0177ed3ae384",
                                        "entry_id": "bae478e3-cc06-30b1-803e-874d679236d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Supporting or representing the Soviet Union or Sovietism; Sovietist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51f55b7c-7e38-4e33-9b25-6bccd21a5c39",
                                                "sense_id": "d670df6c-a18c-3ace-95c3-0177ed3ae384",
                                                "text": "He remained more Soviet than his parents and often accused Gorbachev of having destroyed the Soviet Union on behalf of US intelligence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce80f76b-980f-4f4a-8e41-20c026974d32",
                                                "sense_id": "d670df6c-a18c-3ace-95c3-0177ed3ae384",
                                                "text": "Only in the GDR were the returning POWs presumed guilty; there East Germans, attempting to be \"more Soviet than the Soviets,\" […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "798b68e7-f448-4d4d-a5f0-fbfb064e155a",
                                                "sense_id": "d670df6c-a18c-3ace-95c3-0177ed3ae384",
                                                "text": "It would also be incorrect to creat a \"scale of Sovietism\", arguing, say, that Gildin was more Soviet than Litvakov, or that Litvakov was more Soviet than Dobrushin. Essentially, they were equally Soviet, even if they saw their Sovietism rather differently: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
